  <tr class="best"><td>v109</td><td class="r">77.61</td><td class="r">22.91</td><td class="r">53.736</td><td>+ genus-level backoff</td></tr>
</table>

<h3><span class="num">6.2</span>Where the remaining error is</h3>

<p>The gate separates the two populations almost perfectly on held-out data — AUC
<span class="n">0.981</span> — but only <span class="n">0.911</span> on evaluation. The difference
is the framing shift of §3: the gate reads crops whose statistics move under it. At the deployed
operating point it mis-routes <b>15.9%</b> of images, each then choosing from a candidate set that
cannot contain its label. Correcting only the routing, recognisers fixed, would reach
<span class="n">54.35%</span> — this design's architectural ceiling. Reaching 55% needs
<span class="n">+1.30</span> points from the recognisers themselves (seen-conditional 87.0%→89.6%,
or novel-conditional 29.5%→33.4%), while re-ranking headroom is bounded at ~0.65 by §5.3's anchor.
The gap needs a stronger recogniser, not a better decision rule.</p>

<h2><span class="num">7</span>Conclusion</h2>

<p>Fine-grained, long-tailed and open-set recognition are usually studied separately; this benchmark
forces all three at once, under a rule that denies the system any knowledge of which regime an image
is in. Our answer is a two-route pipeline whose only decision point is a learned quota gate over
evidence the pipeline already computes, with leak-free per-candidate re-ranking on each route:
<span class="n">53.736%</span>, from <span class="n">45.39%</span>.</p>

<p>Three findings should outlast the leaderboard. In a routed open-set system, evidence new to the
router compounds, while re-weighted evidence returns most of what it appears to gain — measured
twice in each direction. Open-set validation pools leak in a way class-disjoint cross-validation
cannot see: a +13-point proxy gain was worth +0.006, and the defence is not a better estimator but a
candidate pool in which every candidate could have been the answer. And where a rule admits more
than one reading, measure the cost of the strict reading and ship it alongside, so the decision
belongs to the organisers rather than to us.</p>

